TITLE:: FluiditySimplePlayer
summary:: Play a FluidModel slice with a simple envelope
categories:: Libraries>FluidModel
related:: Classes/FluidModel

DESCRIPTION::
FluiditySimplePlayer holds envelope settings and makes a function that plays one slice of a link::Classes/FluidModel:: from its link::Classes/FluidModel#-buffer::, mixed to stereo with link::Classes/Splay::, on output bus 0. link::Classes/FluidModel#-play:: uses one with the default settings (no fade in or out).

The envelope lasts exactly one slice. Attack and release are given as fractions of the slice duration, so the same settings fit short and long slices.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
returns:: A FluiditySimplePlayer with code::atk = 0, rls = 0, catk = 0, crls = 0, amp = 1::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: get
Make the play function.

returns:: A link::Classes/Function:: code::{ |corpus, slice, loop = false| ... }:: that plays code::slice:: (an identifier such as code::'drums-12'::) of the link::Classes/FluidModel:: code::corpus:: and returns the link::Classes/Synth::. The envelope settings are read when the function is called. With code::loop:: code::false:: the synth frees itself after one slice. With code::loop:: code::true:: it restarts the slice and its envelope forever, until you free it.

METHOD:: atk
Attack time as a fraction of the slice duration (0 to 1).

METHOD:: rls
Release time as a fraction of the slice duration. code::atk + rls:: should not exceed 1.

METHOD:: catk
Curvature of the attack segment (see link::Classes/Env::).

METHOD:: crls
Curvature of the release segment.

METHOD:: amp
Output gain.

METHOD:: rand
Pick random values for code::atk::, code::rls::, code::catk:: and code::crls:: (code::amp:: is kept).

EXAMPLES::

code::
// needs a built or loaded FluidModel, see its help file
~model = FluidModel(\flucoma);

(
~player = FluiditySimplePlayer().atk_(0.05).rls_(0.6).crls_(-4).amp_(0.5);
~play = ~player.get;
)

~play.(~model, 'flucoma-10');

// loop a slice, then stop it
~loop = ~play.(~model, 'flucoma-10', true);
~loop.free;

// a random envelope for every slice
(
Routine {
	20.do {
		var slice = ~model.slice_cache.keys.choose;
		~player.rand;
		~play.(~model, slice);
		0.3.wait;
	};
}.play;
)

// play the slice under the mouse in a plot, one slice at a time:
// the function returns the Synth, so the previous one can be stopped
(
var last, synth;
~model.plot(\mfcc, action: { |model, slice|
	if (slice != last) {
		last = slice;
		if (synth.notNil and: { synth.isPlaying }) { synth.free };
		synth = ~play.(model, slice).register(true); // register: keep isPlaying up to date
	};
});
)
::
